{"ok":true,"canonical_id":"AUTOSAR/CP/record/SWS_LDCOM_00057","versions":[{"version_id":"AUTOSAR/CP/record/SWS_LDCOM_00057@rel:R21-11#55df19dd","canonical_id":"AUTOSAR/CP/record/SWS_LDCOM_00057","release":"R21-11","content":"When called by its users (e.g. RTE, SwCluC LdCom Proxy), LdCom shall use the Signal Id (\"id\" parameter in the call) as LdComHandleId ( ECUC_LdCom_00005 ), to look - up the correct LdComIPdu in the LdCom configuration. Using the LdComPduRef configuration parameter ( ECUC_LdCom_00010 ) the co rresponding PDU Id in the PduR'S configuration shall be derived. This PDU Id shall then be used when forwarding the call towards the PduR.","meta":{"trigger_kind":"multi_release_ingest","source_pdf":"AUTOSAR_SWS_LargeDataCOM.pdf"},"recorded_at":"2026-09-30T16:45:22+00:00","text_key":"019021e9d847"},{"version_id":"AUTOSAR/CP/record/SWS_LdCom_00057@rel:R22-11#1564a30a","canonical_id":"AUTOSAR/CP/record/SWS_LdCom_00057","release":"R22-11","content":"When called by its users (e.g. RTE, SwCluC LdCom Proxy), LdCom shall use the Signal Id (\"id\" parameter in the call) as LdComHandleId (ECUC_LdCom_00005), to look-up the correct LdComIPdu in the LdCom configura- tion. Using the LdComPduRef configuration parameter (ECUC_LdCom_00010) the corresponding PDU Id in the PduR'S configuration shall be derived. This PDU Id shall then be used when forwarding the call towards the PduR.","meta":{"trigger_kind":"multi_release_ingest","source_pdf":"AUTOSAR_SWS_LargeDataCOM.pdf"},"recorded_at":"2026-10-01T10:13:16+00:00","text_key":"019021e9d847"},{"canonical_id":"AUTOSAR/CP/record/SWS_LDCOM_00057","release":"R24-11","text_captured":false,"meta":{"trigger_kind":"pdf_presence","source":"classic_upstream"}}],"lifecycle":{"canonical_id":"AUTOSAR/CP/record/SWS_LDCOM_00057","is_dropped":false,"first_active_release":"R21-11","last_active_release":"R24-11","dropped_in":[],"first_dropped_release":null,"absent_before":["R18-10","R19-11","R20-11"],"platform_releases":["R18-10","R19-11","R20